# heightfield_strata

- Label: HeightField Strata
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 3
- Parameters: 63 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/heightfield_strata.html
- Summary (EN): HeightField Strata adds rock- or sediment-like layering to a heightfield. It can stack several strata layers with different tilts and rotations.
- Résumé (FR) : HeightField Strata ajoute des strates de type roche ou sédiment à une hauteur, en empilant plusieurs couches inclinées et tournées.

- Inputs meaning: ["height: heightfield that receives the strata", "baseheight: optional extra height that deforms the strata pattern", "mask: optional per-pixel mask, scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Mask: how much strata noise mixes into the height input", "Blend Mode: Add, Subtract, Multiply, Difference, Maximum or Minimum", "Output Strata Only: outputs the strata layer without blending it with height", "Amplitude and Center: scale and offset the strata noise", "Noise Contrast: increases extremeness inside the noise before Amplitude and Center", "Noise Type: base noise function, such as Simplex, Perlin, Worley variants or Sparse Convolution", "Element Size and Offset: size and position of the base noise pattern", "Strata Size and Strata Offset: layer thickness and position", "Tilt and Rotate (with Origin): angle of the layers and their rotation centre", "Add Layers, Layers, Roughness, Tilt Variance, Rotate Variance, Seed: several strata layers with randomization", "Base Height Influence: how strongly baseheight affects the pattern", "Fractal Type, Max Octaves, Lacunarity, Octave Offset, Roughness: finer detail through successive noise octaves", "Post Processing, applied in order: Fold, Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum"]

- Caveats: ["Worley Jitter values above 1 can produce artifacts, because points may jitter past the search radius", "Complement assumes values from 0 to 1; other values can become negative or out of range", "Fold has no effect when all values are positive", "Noise Contrast (inside the noise function) differs from the post-processing Contrast", "The page does not document performance characteristics or other limits"]

